-> There are mainly 8 locators in selenium to find the element in a web page= ID, Name, ClassName, LinkText, PartialLinkText, TagName, XPath,
CSS Selector
-> object.findElemnet(By.____());
-> There are 6 basic controls in html, textbox, link, Button, Radio Button, CheckBox, DropDown
-> If we wanna test Textboxes in a web using webdriver we will get by using web elements.

******************************************X-PATH**********************************************

-> XPath(XML path language) is a query language for selecting nodes from an XML doc or finding element in HTML web page.
-> Xpath is a dynamic locator in Selenium to find elements.


 -- Types of XPath
 -> Absolute XPath- Starts from root element of the document. starts with single '/'
 -> Relative XPath- starts from any point in the document. starts with double '//' (Recommended)

XPath using Attributes
 =>XPath using attributes by Relative Path- //tagName[@attribute = 'value']
 -> tag-name- input, button, div, span....etc
 -> AttributeName- type, id, name, class, value...etc

 XPath Operators (=, !=, <,<=,>, >= etc) used for elements having similar fields with different signatures.

 XPath Conditions mainly consists of "and", "or", "not".

 XPath Index

XPath Functions= XPath provides some predefined functions to find elements mainly 6
-> Text, Normalize-space, Contains, Last, starts-With, Position
->  //tagName[text()='value'] syntax
-> //tagName[contains(text(),'value')] syntax

 XPath Axes these are all DOM modifiers for XPath in html
 Ancestor-> ancestor, ancestor-or-self
 Descendant-> Descendant, Descendant-or-self
 Sibling-> preceding-Sibling, following-Sibling
 parent-> parent
 Child-> child
 Syntax:- //tagname[@Attribute=value]/modifier::tagname[@Attribute=value]


 XPath Shortcuts/ Abbreviations

-> [text()=='']==> [.='']   we can use '.' for text

-> child::==> / we can use '/' in place of child
-> parent:: ==> /.. we uses .. after / for parent